shammy (0.15.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Generated images use 10 sampling steps, matching zimage-gw: a blind
    comparison found them visibly better. Normal quality now takes about
    5 min and max about 12 min, and the image tool tells the model so.

 -- Bryan Christ <bryan.christ@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 15:21:31 -0600

shammy (0.15.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Generated images are drawn at the gateway's max quality by default (about
    1 megapixel, about 10 min). "normal quality", "quickly" or "fast" give
    the 768-pixel, 8-step render (about 4 to 5 min) instead.
  * Upscale 2x and Upscale 4x under each generated image ask zimage-gw for an
    ESRGAN upscale. The upscale shows beneath the original, which is kept,
    each with its own Save as..., Copy and viewer. Nothing upscales
    automatically any more.
  * Save as... offers a dated name (shammy-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS.png), starts in
    the home folder, then in the folder last saved to while Shammy runs.
  * The chat no longer snaps back down while you scroll up past a tall image
    or a streaming reply; sending a message or opening another chat returns
    to the end.
  * Unit tests are left out of the default build; build them with the
    "tests" target before running ctest.

 -- Bryan Christ <bryan.christ@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 10:36:32 -0600

shammy (0.15.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Image generation: with a zimage-gw server set in Settings -> Image
    generation and Tools on, the model can call generate_image. Progress
    (queue, stage, percent, time left) shows in the thread; the PNG and a
    JSON sidecar are saved under the data folder's images/, with Save as...
    and Copy. Stop cancels the job on the server.
  * Clicking a generated image opens a pop-out viewer: zoom (+, -, wheel,
    drag to pan), Fit (0), Copy (Ctrl+C), Full screen (f), and a control bar
    that fades out when the mouse rests.
  * A caption after a tool result is no longer followed by a re-prompt and
    apologies about missing artifacts.

 -- Bryan Christ <bryan.christ@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:56:46 -0600

shammy (0.14.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Agent skills: SKILL.md folders under ~/.config/shammy/skills (macOS:
    ~/Library/Application Support/shammy/skills, then ~/.config), loaded by
    the model with the new load_skill tool; new Settings -> Skills page.
  * Shell commands for the model (run_command), off by default; every command
    is approved first, once or for the chat, and stopped after 120 s or Stop.
  * Ollama backends are sent chats on Ollama's own /api/chat, so the context
    size set per model is what Ollama loads the model with.
  * Clearer message when Ollama refuses tools or thinking for a model.
  * "Hide from selection" per model keeps it out of the model picker.
  * Header model drop-down: long names fit, themed list, current model bold.
  * "Once" in the MCP permission dialog now allows only that call.

 -- Bryan Christ <bryan.christ@gmail.com>  Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:12:33 -0500

